        "original_id": "d4dd2f77-9cc5-5454-94b8-22c936dbef09",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Double\n- Products: Blue, Dou3le, \"The Captain of Her Heart\", \"Woman of the World\", \"Rangoon Moon\", \"Devils Ball\"\n- Places: Europe\n- Concepts: hit singles, album releases\n\nFacts:\n- Double was a Swiss music duo pronounced \"doo-blay.\"\n- In 1986, Double released \"The Captain of Her Heart\" as a single, and it became an immediate success throughout Europe.\n- \"The Captain of Her Heart\" was a plaintive, atmospheric, piano-led ballad and became Double's best-known hit single.\n- The album Blue included updated versions of Double's earlier singles \"Woman of the World\" and \"Rangoon Moon.\"\n- The album Blue included the international smash hit \"The Captain of Her Heart.\"\n- \"Devils Ball\" is a song by Double that was released as the lead single from the band's second studio album Dou3le.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "439ceb15-8cda-5b68-a5c8-2a4ae97e6198",
        "text": "Page: Blue (Double album). Sentence: In addition to containing updated versions of two of the band's earlier singles (\"Woman of the World\" and \"Rangoon Moon\"), the album included the international smash hit, \"The Captain of Her Heart\", a plaintive, atmospheric, piano-led ballad which was an immediate success throughout Europe upon its 1986 single release.\nPage: Double (band). Sentence: Double (pronounced \"doo-blay\") was a Swiss music duo best known for their hit single \"The Captain of Her Heart\".\nPage: Devils Ball. Sentence: \"Devils Ball\" is a song by Swiss duo Double, released as the lead single from their second studio album \"Dou3le\".",
